# CRM SaaS Template — Core

This is a **Next.js Pages Router frontend CRM template** (demo data, no live DB). Sellable UI kit, not a production backend.

## Stack (do not change without asking)
- Next.js 12 Pages Router · React 17 · Tailwind · shadcn/ui (`components/ui/`) · Lucide · sonner
- Data: in-memory `utils/CrmDataContext.jsx` + `*SeedData.js` — **not** Supabase/Firebase yet
- Theme: `useTheme()` + Theme Customizer CSS vars — see `Design.md`
- Deep context: `llm.txt` · Design: `Design.md`

## Dual surfaces
| Surface | Routes | Layout |
|---------|--------|--------|
| Agency marketing | `/`, `/pricing`, `/faq`, `/contact` | `disableLayout = true` · `AgencySite/` |
| CRM app | `/demo`, `/leads`, `/deals`, … | `modules/Layout` (sidebar + navbar) |

Never mix Agency Gumroad copy into buyer-facing CRM modules.

## Non-negotiables
- Thin routes: `pages/foo.js` → export from `app/Foo`
- Register nav in `modules/navConfig.js` only
- Prefer shadcn + `FormModal` / `FormSelect` / `ExportDropdown`
- Icons: `lucide-react` (brand icons: `react-icons` only when needed)
- Toasts: `sonner`
- Match existing file style; minimize scope; no drive-by refactors

## Do not
- Invent a backend or connect Supabase/Firebase unless the user asks (see `crm-backend-later` rule)
- Add `/agent-ops` without creating the page (or remove the nav item)
- Hard-code a single accent color in feature modules — use `useTheme()` / CSS tokens
- Dump 60+ screens of unrelated verticals into one flat nav
